     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu saw a bean seed grow into a plant over two weeks.\n\"Plants breathe too,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "respiration",
     "stomata",
     "growth"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Plants grow from seeds into seedlings and then into mature plants by getting water, nutrients from the soil and food made by leaves. Growth happens mainly at the tips of roots and shoots.\nPlants respire all the time, taking in oxygen and giving out carbon dioxide, using stomata in leaves.\nIn daytime photosynthesis is more than respiration, so the plant gives out more oxygen than it takes in."
    }
